{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJgbXEpSh1CZwntxm5DP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the crash, and both tests now pass when I run `python3 -m unittest`.\n\n- **Crash:** The cause was in `ingest/reader.py`, not in the analytics code. It read the CSV using `;` as the separator, but the shop uploads use commas. The file's own comment says so, and so does `data/sales.csv`. Because of that, the column `amount` was never found and the report crashed. I changed the reader to use the default comma separator. The average ticket now comes out to 10000.\n- **Unit:** `UNIT` in `analytics/stats.py` is now `\"CLP\"`.\n\nThe reader fix is in the ingest module, which is outside the analytics code. Anything else that uses `rows()` will now also read files with commas. Because the comment says the uploads are comma-separated, that should be correct. But if some source really does send `;`-separated files, whoever owns ingest should check it.\n\nI haven't committed the changes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":876,"cache_read_input_tokens":22297,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":876},"output_tokens":302,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e5bb60b0-8fde-426e-993a-d835ab4bfc9e","uuid":"80c5ef10-0dcf-422a-a707-c7da5de52b26","timestamp":"2026-10-23T06:19:17.763Z","request_id":"req_011CgJgbWyhQxEWKwccPgbjX"}
